===================================================================================================
Data-derived file: the public draft token map (tokenmaps/public/)
===================================================================================================

tokenmaps/public/public_49152.pt is a sorted list of 49,152 token ids of the Qwen3.8-Flash-Next
tokenizer, ranked by how often each id occurs when public text is tokenised. It contains no text,
no counts and no other content of the sources; public_49152.sources.json records which files were
read (repository, revision, file, sha256, licence) and the per-source document, character and token
totals. Whether a frequency-ranked id list is an adaptation of the source text under the
ShareAlike licence of Wikipedia is not settled. To be safe, these two data files are offered under
the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/) instead of Apache-2.0, with the attributions
below. The scripts that build the map (tokenmaps/public/fetch_public.sh,
tokenmaps/public/prep_public.py, tokenmaps/build_hot_vocab.py) are Apache-2.0 like the rest of
the repository; they download the sources from their publishers and redistribute none of them.

Changes made to every source: the files listed below were read once (conversations: only the
assistant / "gpt" / "ai" turns; capped at a fixed number of characters per source, in file order),
tokenised, and only the per-token frequencies were used to rank the ids.

